<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηπτουχία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing of a staff</i> or
				<i>sceptre</i> as the badge of command, hence <i>military
				command</i>, esp. of the Persians, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ σκηπτουχίᾳ ταχθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					297
				</span></i>
			; technically, <i>rank</i> or <i>province of a Persian</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηπτοῦχος</span> (v. sq. <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.2.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>command, power</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				111
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
